msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Performance materiality"
msgstr "績效重大性"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid ""
"The performance materiality, also known the intolerable deviation rate or "
"intolerable misstatement (sometimes tolerable deviation rate or "
"misstatement), is a value established by the auditor that is below, or equal "
"to, the overall materiality of the financial statements. Typically in an "
"audit, the performance materiality is set lower than the overall materiality "
"to reduce the chance that the total of undetected misstatements exceeds the "
"materiality of the financial statements as a whole. In this analysis, the "
"performance materiality represents the lowest unacceptable level of "
"misstatement in the population being tested. By enabling this sampling "
"objective, you can design a sample to determine whether the population as a "
"whole contain misstatements that are deemed material (i.e. are greater or "
"equal to the performance materiality) while respecting a certain audit risk "
"(1 - confidence level). The value of the performance materiality affects the "
"minimum sample size. A lower performance materiality requires a relatively "
"larger minimum sample size to reduce the audit risk to an acceptably low "
"level, while a higher performance materiality requires a relatively smaller "
"sample size to reduce the audit risk to an acceptably low level."
msgstr ""
"績效重大性，又稱不可容忍偏差率或不可容忍錯報（有時是可容忍偏差率或錯報），是"
"由審計師所設定、低於或等於財務報表整體重大性之數值。在審計中，績效重大性通常"
"設定得低於整體重大性，以降低未偵測錯報總額超過整個財務報表之重大性的機率。在"
"此分析中，績效重大性代表所檢定母體中不可接受之最低錯報水準。藉由啟用此抽樣目"
"標，您可以設計一個樣本，以在尊重特定審計風險 (1 - 信賴水準) 的同時，判定整體"
"母體是否包含被視為重大（即大於或等於績效重大性）之錯報。績效重大性之數值會影"
"響最小樣本規模。較低的績效重大性需要相對較大的最小樣本規模，以將審計風險降至"
"可接受之低水準；較高的績效重大性則需要相對較小的樣本規模。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Specify how the performance materiality is defined."
msgstr "指定績效重大性如何定義。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Relative"
msgstr "相對"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid ""
"Specify the performance materiality as a percentage relative to the total "
"number of units in the population."
msgstr "以佔母體單位總數之百分比的相對形式指定績效重大性。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "The percentage associated with the performance materiality."
msgstr "與績效重大性關聯之百分比。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Absolute"
msgstr "絕對"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid ""
"Specify the performance materiality as an absolute value in monetary units."
msgstr "以貨幣單位之絕對數值形式指定績效重大性。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "The value associated with the performance materiality."
msgstr "與績效重大性關聯之數值。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Click to learn more about this objective"
msgstr "按一下以進一步了解此目標"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Minimum precision"
msgstr "最小精確度"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid ""
"The precision is a measure of how much uncertainty there is in the estimate "
"of the misstatement in the population at a given level of sampling risk. "
"Typically in an audit, the precision is used to determine if enough work has "
"been performed to effectively estimate the misstatement in the population. "
"In this analysis, the precision represents the difference between the "
"estimated most likely misstatement in the population and the upper bound of "
"the misstatement in the population. By enabling this sampling objective, you "
"can design a sample that minimizes the difference between the estimated most "
"likely misstatement and the upper bound of the misstatement to a certain "
"percentage. The value of the minimum precision affects the minimum sample "
"size. A smaller minimum required precision will result in a larger sample "
"size, while a higher minimum required precision will result in a smaller "
"sample size."
msgstr ""
"精確度是在給定之抽樣風險水準下，母體錯報估計中不確定性程度之量測。在審計中，"
"精確度通常用於判定是否已完成足夠之工作，以有效估計母體錯報。在此分析中，精確"
"度代表母體中最可能錯報之估計與母體錯報上界之間的差異。藉由啟用此抽樣目標，您"
"可以設計一個樣本，以將最可能錯報估計與錯報上界之間的差異最小化至特定百分比。"
"最小精確度之數值會影響最小樣本規模。較小之所需最小精確度會導致較大的樣本規"
"模，較高之所需最小精確度則會導致較小的樣本規模。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "The percentage associated with the minimum precision."
msgstr "與最小精確度關聯之百分比。"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid "Confidence"
msgstr "信賴水準"

msgctxt "SamplingObjectives|"
msgid ""
"The confidence level used. The confidence level is the complement of the "
"audit risk: the risk that the user is willing to take to give an incorrect "
"judgment about the population. For example, if you want to use an audit risk "
"of 5%, this equals 95% confidence."
msgstr ""
"所使用的信賴水準。信賴水準是審計風險之補數：使用者願意承擔對母體作出錯誤判斷"
"的風險。例如，若您想使用 5% 的審計風險，這相當於 95% 的信賴水準。"

